[{:db/id "q-158025/selection/1d6e8248d14b6e31ca2641d833d84096fddc7999b7658316d682d85169821f82" :answer/id #uuid "564def48-6013-59e6-9baf-190b7104df0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158025/selection/b431c224fe4d08a5a26b85ed0e9a1b3cc6b6ca194b2fc9fe253ec7c83d5f2800" :answer/id #uuid "bb32a9d2-9e67-5063-ab6f-b3b6a29ddb6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158025/selection/0262bd006635f29d90133924e85299f10a959a46d70b799edce59f78e6ee19e5" :answer/id #uuid "8c749822-94c7-5c64-8c64-4c6266ddfeb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158025/selection/a2e004f5d1f8b93a1aae88857cd5d4c2cb7850c1178f908d7686ffa2e2439ef1" :answer/id #uuid "5fe54718-6808-5e7a-a523-0f7ed9bb0994" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158025/selection/9ceb8555ac642f761bd0d5541e7cece978f71e0796f7c77524dac24125cb1408" :answer/id #uuid "38df9078-ba5c-5fad-b6cd-04e7a2c8eb0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158025/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d798e2d-0f06-548c-a16c-b2ee7dde6f1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158025/selection/b431c224fe4d08a5a26b85ed0e9a1b3cc6b6ca194b2fc9fe253ec7c83d5f2800" :answer-field/choices ["q-158025/selection/1d6e8248d14b6e31ca2641d833d84096fddc7999b7658316d682d85169821f82" "q-158025/selection/b431c224fe4d08a5a26b85ed0e9a1b3cc6b6ca194b2fc9fe253ec7c83d5f2800" "q-158025/selection/0262bd006635f29d90133924e85299f10a959a46d70b799edce59f78e6ee19e5" "q-158025/selection/a2e004f5d1f8b93a1aae88857cd5d4c2cb7850c1178f908d7686ffa2e2439ef1" "q-158025/selection/9ceb8555ac642f761bd0d5541e7cece978f71e0796f7c77524dac24125cb1408"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158025" :question/id #uuid "ba587f1b-dab3-553a-b4db-544d035b8b45" :question/math-academy-id "q-158025" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{y}^{3}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-158025/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d908f1-591e-5cb6-afc5-fa7ec44ec326"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158025"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-154357/selection/1a087ecdc38208058d4744c3ceab97582252ca7f2cd2c195d95af2a8c14384e1" :answer/id #uuid "2d194fc1-1b54-547d-811f-8c77414c1ee5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-154357/selection/bfbdcd06452c01fa475e4ffb209925aa469f7ab53b6632e2d6f6b7b8cbadb200" :answer/id #uuid "31493b54-06f9-5e3e-9f8e-15343c3c84f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-154357/selection/84480105686a73a3658aac0df9085de56f22c3b91d57fca48802cb6e3607ebb3" :answer/id #uuid "ec29e029-fed1-5d53-a9e3-813ab000e0f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-154357/selection/133e2c5b706ee9498dae23fcf6a0ffa757d6a88fc43d623272c022a45d850849" :answer/id #uuid "03daf3fe-5900-5737-94b7-8be50d710f85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-154357/selection/5309229b372eb5d29edd0501ae2e5d294be7a32ea09f6be5e69ccb7ad043daf0" :answer/id #uuid "030e2cbd-9d58-5290-b1d9-91417538f250" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-154357/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "52ecedda-ee36-5ee3-93e0-3e3fb3da0ef2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-154357/selection/5309229b372eb5d29edd0501ae2e5d294be7a32ea09f6be5e69ccb7ad043daf0" :answer-field/choices ["q-154357/selection/1a087ecdc38208058d4744c3ceab97582252ca7f2cd2c195d95af2a8c14384e1" "q-154357/selection/bfbdcd06452c01fa475e4ffb209925aa469f7ab53b6632e2d6f6b7b8cbadb200" "q-154357/selection/84480105686a73a3658aac0df9085de56f22c3b91d57fca48802cb6e3607ebb3" "q-154357/selection/133e2c5b706ee9498dae23fcf6a0ffa757d6a88fc43d623272c022a45d850849" "q-154357/selection/5309229b372eb5d29edd0501ae2e5d294be7a32ea09f6be5e69ccb7ad043daf0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-154357" :question/id #uuid "fed70404-5aaf-52d2-8686-4c656a529df4" :question/math-academy-id "q-154357" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y}$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-154357/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-154357"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-118885/selection/55c002f60cb8d6d32d1895ee6466694a820f8134dacd04358cc37e045721b426" :answer/id #uuid "ab3e08a0-05d6-5f27-be05-eb7635d17b5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118885/selection/352aa1c27a42bea48f62846321a79c70519ec7febdf4f899a4f842292f67d2dd" :answer/id #uuid "f82833d6-76e7-526f-8690-513b935ffc80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118885/selection/c677b9f80e417908f60db2f77c992408d0a76b2548759881db7d44f4d32b5b64" :answer/id #uuid "534e3799-1c4d-5051-a2f0-cee6bd143819" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118885/selection/ce1d04bbc49e6b997e72ef6c3b65a8db5ca3cd842460da93793f8cce66562245" :answer/id #uuid "08b86fa1-74c1-52ae-9d88-a7f80bc9f7e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=2{e}^{x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118885/selection/62ca9a349f01166843ea6ac4213b1f61b0908cea592aaa006fc562fe65786847" :answer/id #uuid "28ea0db4-a307-51b9-8d43-26c6d713de6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{2x}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118885/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3226a4d-2e16-5c47-adc4-39cfe15f3aad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-118885/selection/c677b9f80e417908f60db2f77c992408d0a76b2548759881db7d44f4d32b5b64" :answer-field/choices ["q-118885/selection/55c002f60cb8d6d32d1895ee6466694a820f8134dacd04358cc37e045721b426" "q-118885/selection/352aa1c27a42bea48f62846321a79c70519ec7febdf4f899a4f842292f67d2dd" "q-118885/selection/c677b9f80e417908f60db2f77c992408d0a76b2548759881db7d44f4d32b5b64" "q-118885/selection/ce1d04bbc49e6b997e72ef6c3b65a8db5ca3cd842460da93793f8cce66562245" "q-118885/selection/62ca9a349f01166843ea6ac4213b1f61b0908cea592aaa006fc562fe65786847"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118885" :question/id #uuid "f6a01c34-9b8c-5742-a002-5656bbb5e9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-118885" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y$ for $0<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}{cos}^{2}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & ={e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={e}^{x}+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118885/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a67b149c-f701-5be0-868d-c2f4a4be4be4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118885"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-14244"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-158017/selection/3550ba86141b6268662088ced5774ad0c519934b21079874e0daaa924b3f0c78" :answer/id #uuid "89cb340f-0478-584c-b2ef-13f05abef887" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158017/selection/8e90fc20257e03be8590185566b4ddc47518c954ca44c653865e0409123a0797" :answer/id #uuid "11a47ba4-f242-5f17-967a-c31ff9f17190" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158017/selection/5d7115d2cd242b378e093cad6023ae5806acc1ebdae4d2e1655f121adedad8e9" :answer/id #uuid "7c5bca59-1c2d-504d-ba7c-a8b66a6a82eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158017/selection/e5e7f0d1d0d91599777b1abd2bcc3677877b76c40b9a6824235042b58bfa19aa" :answer/id #uuid "c03d2759-88bd-5b8a-885b-23c829ab9bdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158017/selection/4515c78df58c9460189031fa2a003357e56bf45f69a34780d06f9f0da11b4e88" :answer/id #uuid "34609bcf-9819-55ba-9ad6-58492df84acb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158017/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c763e14-0bd0-5572-8ef8-79991bf0d840" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158017/selection/5d7115d2cd242b378e093cad6023ae5806acc1ebdae4d2e1655f121adedad8e9" :answer-field/choices ["q-158017/selection/3550ba86141b6268662088ced5774ad0c519934b21079874e0daaa924b3f0c78" "q-158017/selection/8e90fc20257e03be8590185566b4ddc47518c954ca44c653865e0409123a0797" "q-158017/selection/5d7115d2cd242b378e093cad6023ae5806acc1ebdae4d2e1655f121adedad8e9" "q-158017/selection/e5e7f0d1d0d91599777b1abd2bcc3677877b76c40b9a6824235042b58bfa19aa" "q-158017/selection/4515c78df58c9460189031fa2a003357e56bf45f69a34780d06f9f0da11b4e88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158017" :question/id #uuid "ac44d433-a7db-5b48-a5c5-fbb14f94435f" :question/math-academy-id "q-158017" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-158017/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158017"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-3854/selection/eccca557b74dfc854d9ab736c14a31dc7179d3ddc972661e97e87d07f40e300a" :answer/id #uuid "810d8ae3-e659-552e-991f-6b14f26edca2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3854/selection/7915a3266598c41e4be80b6a0ea4a575bd610f76802af4e368e83c1e88ee213a" :answer/id #uuid "f115aba7-d8f5-5d0b-8c18-05b7b59d2bc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{2}}+{e}^{{x}^{3}}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3854/selection/683b299dc09b2ade72036e3e49ebbaa469c79b83c5217298effd213ca3cc589b" :answer/id #uuid "ad4aa770-c8f3-5ef3-8ef4-ac28d2806dd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3854/selection/42309a1aac507d0430a33e33bdc7b68841e321b2ddd2eade34c10b5522ad5b33" :answer/id #uuid "095c386d-e826-5ea2-a5fb-30f72af48e88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3854/selection/c76597508706597483008c8c57e471d8875d274dfa9934a6d02ad2af189b36ea" :answer/id #uuid "bce41ee9-5b15-52f9-8585-7ad4ee731284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{3}+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3854/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d6f149e-7d48-587b-8cb2-9be31ecbf0be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-3854/selection/42309a1aac507d0430a33e33bdc7b68841e321b2ddd2eade34c10b5522ad5b33" :answer-field/choices ["q-3854/selection/eccca557b74dfc854d9ab736c14a31dc7179d3ddc972661e97e87d07f40e300a" "q-3854/selection/7915a3266598c41e4be80b6a0ea4a575bd610f76802af4e368e83c1e88ee213a" "q-3854/selection/683b299dc09b2ade72036e3e49ebbaa469c79b83c5217298effd213ca3cc589b" "q-3854/selection/42309a1aac507d0430a33e33bdc7b68841e321b2ddd2eade34c10b5522ad5b33" "q-3854/selection/c76597508706597483008c8c57e471d8875d274dfa9934a6d02ad2af189b36ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-3854" :question/id #uuid "c533f957-5ce4-560a-af3f-547368ddc163" :question/math-academy-id "q-3854" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-3854/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3854"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-14247/selection/e424cfde5a697e5f2c9d699f70855797b7a0731fd2098f2854bb5c22746cd95d" :answer/id #uuid "1c36ba58-cea6-5f95-bafc-9814cf59d93a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14247/selection/fe3baa6d537ad76c168811272893e7ec04a8b5b43896254712206459a042b727" :answer/id #uuid "d22f4e71-4ecc-5851-886f-48f02106a8aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}+2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14247/selection/b9fa8378c1a8213964b48308ab2809c026ec7caf41998faaecdf0b919bb0e5f5" :answer/id #uuid "3e44b657-91bd-589b-a1d1-611d26d8f603" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14247/selection/5a046595f225048254707ab8164ab48fe0404a481d093dcf73f47b486dec6b38" :answer/id #uuid "a2398db1-88c9-574c-91fa-70c569652e09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{3{x}^{2}+x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14247/selection/94afc5b6defce437c068185bd152e832ded1bc1a15acc2626f3c93a415ef75a8" :answer/id #uuid "5415f72f-9dd4-53d1-8dc6-09655c362101" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14247/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6725044-65b4-5d9c-9e33-f0f0efa45de9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14247/selection/94afc5b6defce437c068185bd152e832ded1bc1a15acc2626f3c93a415ef75a8" :answer-field/choices ["q-14247/selection/e424cfde5a697e5f2c9d699f70855797b7a0731fd2098f2854bb5c22746cd95d" "q-14247/selection/fe3baa6d537ad76c168811272893e7ec04a8b5b43896254712206459a042b727" "q-14247/selection/b9fa8378c1a8213964b48308ab2809c026ec7caf41998faaecdf0b919bb0e5f5" "q-14247/selection/5a046595f225048254707ab8164ab48fe0404a481d093dcf73f47b486dec6b38" "q-14247/selection/94afc5b6defce437c068185bd152e832ded1bc1a15acc2626f3c93a415ef75a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14247" :question/id #uuid "321b7d69-9883-59b2-a4d0-4ebf210bb530" :question/math-academy-id "q-14247" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y+3y{x}^{2}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y+3y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y+3y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(1+3{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1+3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =x+{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{3}+x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-14247/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14247"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79666/selection/8a56a7736aa7585e0e1a4cb9614c3db20f4272258b524b0d591495c074c1facb" :answer/id #uuid "5146ed63-5fe6-5163-b942-ab4d2f76fc29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79666/selection/d3ee1b73b662c57b0df80afe5caeaddf410a1ea60189798f3ac13bc6886c2a0c" :answer/id #uuid "b9049a8a-81ee-5b86-84bd-f48f3676fff2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79666/selection/7828b54812f3a9d2549afd072fb751f446b2fe242b186955ab61d08b8bc4780b" :answer/id #uuid "b424038f-53ec-50b8-a577-28ac20132663" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79666/selection/bcc4d856f0045887587cd8b9dec12e054a02bd8b1804f18b724ca05edfc2157d" :answer/id #uuid "44ea5ccd-9db8-5f00-84c6-f669861f31ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79666/selection/e8b9fd37152ffc9bb992fa156edf4bef528b8b931b200ee2d3062c172c44a3e0" :answer/id #uuid "3db25045-43dd-5a7d-b7f1-a13ee117b7c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79666/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8797a9ff-99b0-5fd2-ac06-80813f3e4551" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79666/selection/7828b54812f3a9d2549afd072fb751f446b2fe242b186955ab61d08b8bc4780b" :answer-field/choices ["q-79666/selection/8a56a7736aa7585e0e1a4cb9614c3db20f4272258b524b0d591495c074c1facb" "q-79666/selection/d3ee1b73b662c57b0df80afe5caeaddf410a1ea60189798f3ac13bc6886c2a0c" "q-79666/selection/7828b54812f3a9d2549afd072fb751f446b2fe242b186955ab61d08b8bc4780b" "q-79666/selection/bcc4d856f0045887587cd8b9dec12e054a02bd8b1804f18b724ca05edfc2157d" "q-79666/selection/e8b9fd37152ffc9bb992fa156edf4bef528b8b931b200ee2d3062c172c44a3e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79666" :question/id #uuid "d9f3f4e8-eb82-571e-bb8f-ae7778e94ec7" :question/math-academy-id "q-79666" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y}=0$ for $y>0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2y} \\\\ 2y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2y\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79666/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b784e1-ad0e-5cf2-8b02-604a7098c6a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79666"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
